.TH TSTUI 1 "2026-11-21" "tstui 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tstui \- k9s-style terminal UI for Teleport SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tstui
.RB [ \-\-proxy
.IR HOST:PORT | NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-user
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-password\-stdin " | " \-\-password\-file
.IR PATH " | " \fB\-\-password\fR " " PASS ]
.RB [ \-\-mfa\-token
.IR CODE ]
.RB [ \-\-auth
.IR CONNECTOR ]
.RB [ \-\-insecure ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-skin
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tstui
wraps
.BR tsh (1),
Teleport's command-line client, in a terminal UI. It lists the servers of
the current proxy and its leaf clusters, opens SSH sessions in an embedded
terminal with tabs and split panes, and logs in through a popup that asks
for the user, password and MFA code, or waits for a security key touch.
It also transfers files, runs port forwards, and runs one command on many
servers.
.PP
.B tsh
must be on
.BR PATH .
tstui runs it for everything and never talks to Teleport by itself, except
for the unauthenticated
.I /webapi/ping
health check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " HOST:PORT|NAME"
The Teleport proxy, or the name of a proxy in the config file.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
The Teleport user.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read the password from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " PATH"
Read the password from a file. tstui warns when the file is readable by
other users.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " PASS"
The password. Supported, but tstui prints a warning: the value shows in
shell history and the process list.
.TP
.BI \-\-mfa\-token " CODE"
A one-time code for MFA.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth " CONNECTOR"
The auth connector, as for
.BR "tsh \-\-auth" .
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification. For test clusters only.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
The config file. Default
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tstui/config.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-\-skin " NAME"
.BR default ,
.BR light ,
.BR high\-contrast ,
or a skin file's name.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Anything needed to log in that is not given is asked for in the login
popup, never on the plain terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TSTUI_PROXY ", " TSTUI_USER ", " TSTUI_PASSWORD ", " TSTUI_MFA
Login values. Flags take precedence over the environment, and the
environment over the config file. tstui removes
.B TSTUI_PASSWORD
and
.B TSTUI_MFA
from the environment of every process it starts.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the config and the state files live (defaults
.I ~/.config
and
.IR ~/.local/state ).
.SH KEYS
Press
.B ?
in tstui for every key. The most used:
.TP
.B enter
On the server list: connect, or show the server's open session.
.TP
.B /
Filter the server list, for example
.BR "web env=prod" .
.TP
.B :
Command palette:
.BR :proxy ,
.BR :cluster ,
.BR :ssh ,
.BR :scp ,
.BR :pf ,
.BR :exec ,
.BR :skin ,
.BR :quit .
.TP
.B p
Proxy picker.
.TP
.B ctrl\-b
In the terminal, the prefix key (config
.BR keybindings.focus ).
Then
.B tab
goes to the server list,
.BR | " and " \-
split,
.B 1\-9
picks a tab,
.B d
detaches and
.B q
quits.
.TP
.B alt\-1 ... alt\-9
Switch tabs from anywhere.
.TP
.B q
On the server list: quit (asks first while sessions are open).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tstui/config.yaml
Configuration, mode 0600. See
.I /usr/share/doc/tstui/examples/config.yaml
for every key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tstui/skins/NAME.yaml
Skin files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tstui/
Remembered logins, the server-list cache for offline use, the transfer
log, and the multi-exec audit log. All mode 0600.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on a usage error, 3 after an internal error
(the report is on standard error), and 128 plus the signal number when
stopped by SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tsh (1)
.PP
https://goteleport.com/docs/
